2026-07-25 (later) — OWNER-REPORTED FOLLOW-UPS ON 326/327, BOTH ROOT-CAUSED + FIXED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
✅ 326b "aspect still locked on pgm though editor is correct" (0b327ac):
        mapContentFitToStretch ignored aspectLocked — every non-stretch content
        fit contain-fits media at its OWN aspect inside the rect, so take/nudge
        FILL undid the unlocked rect. Unlock now → stretch (rect wins), both
        server + client mirrors. Relock restores contentFit rules.
✅ 327b "compose preview wrong aspect with custom-res screen" (bad33b3):
        server resolveCellSourceDims read legacy screen_N_mode keys (absent on
        this destinations-configured box) → 1080p default → 2560x896 PGM fitted
        16:9 inside every compose hole. Now screenDestinations first (verified
        against live channelMap). Also timeline-editor now uses the canonical
        getResolutionForScreen chain instead of raw programResolutions.
BOTH need the node restart + kiosk reload to go live (same restart as WO-322 +
WO-329B — one maintenance moment covers all four, with the WO-322 visual check).

2026-07-25 (even later) — 326c: "aspect lock works, but not consistently" on
PRV corner drags. The throttled mixer nudge sent a minimal layer payload
WITHOUT aspectLocked → only the nudge contain-fit while the full push
stretched; two writers raced at throttle boundaries, so the layer
intermittently "jumped back to locked". Payload + nudge dedup key now carry
the lock state (5a947f4). Client-only — kiosk reload. Owner confirmed 327b
(compose-preview aspect) landed after the earlier restart/reload.

326d: with air stretching right, the LOOKS EDITOR canvas was the last holdout —
its draw contain-fit unlocked layers and painted the uncovered rect black. Both
layer draw sites now treat aspectLocked===false as stretch (54bc1e1).
Client-only — kiosk reload. Full unlock chain now consistent end to end:
