2026-07-25 (later) — WO-333: REAL AUDIO REACTIVITY FOR SHADERS (aae22a1)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Owner asked how to feed audio into the shaders; most probable source = line-in
or USB capture. Built the full pipe: arecord (ALSA) → 1024-pt Blackman FFT with
AnalyserNode byte semantics → 30Hz {freq,wave} frames → WS 'audio_fft' →
player.js writes them into the ShaderToy audio texture (OSC loudness synth
stays as the <1.5s-stale fallback; getUserMedia tier A untouched).
- New: src/audio/fft.js, src/audio/audio-capture-fft.js,
  src/bootstrap/audio-capture-lifecycle.js; config key audioCapture →
  config/audio_capture.json (device-local, never replicated).
- USB hotplug: deviceMatch substring re-resolved against arecord -l on every
  retry (2s→30s backoff). Stale PCM → one zero frame (decay to silence).
- Verified live on the box against plughw:0,0 (ALC1220): frames flow, waveform
  centered, noise floor sane. Gate 1521/2, smoke-wo333 (11) added.
TO ACTIVATE (owner): put {"enabled":true,"deviceMatch":"usb"} (or a device
string like "plughw:0,2" for the line-in) in config/audio_capture.json, then
the SAME node restart that's already owed for 322b/329B. Shader templates pick
up the new player.js on their next CG ADD — no build, no kiosk reload.
Note: don't point it at a card a live-audio bridge slot uses (hw single-open;
lifecycle warns). Follow-up candidate if that's ever needed: tee PCM out of
the slot's ffmpeg bridge instead of a second open.
